# Databricks Assessment Isolation

This repo is scoped to the DE C1 assessment only.

## Profile (mandatory)

- **Only** use Databricks profile **`de-assessment-ce`**
- **Host:** `https://dbc-06f970f4-0f19.cloud.databricks.com`
- **Never** use `DEFAULT`, `dev`, `prod`, `uat`, or any non-assessment profile from this workspace
- **Never** omit `--profile` on CLI commands — the user's default CLI profile is not assessment

Before any Databricks CLI, bundle, or MCP action:

1. `source scripts/env.sh` (sets `DATABRICKS_CONFIG_PROFILE` and `DATABRICKS_HOST`)
2. Pass `--profile de-assessment-ce` on every `databricks` CLI invocation

## MCP and plugins

| Integration | Name | Purpose |
|-------------|------|---------|
| MCP server | `databricks-de-assessment` | Workspace tools via AI Dev Kit (profile pinned in `.cursor/mcp.json`) |
| MCP server | `github-de-assessment` | GitHub for **JGirulkar** assessment repo only |
| Plugin | `databricks` | Skills routing (`databricks-core`, product skills) |
| Plugin | `superpowers` | Process skills (brainstorming, plans, debugging) |
| Plugin | `github` | **Disabled** — use `github-de-assessment` MCP instead |

## Databricks task routing

Load `databricks-core` first, then the matching product skill (jobs, dabs, unity-catalog, etc.). Do not run ad hoc Databricks commands without skills guidance.
